			<item>
				<title>Spockify - Part 1</title>
				<link>/posts/spockify-part-1/</link>
				<pubDate>Wed, 26 May 2021 13:23:04 -0700</pubDate>
				<guid>/posts/spockify-part-1/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;I&amp;rsquo;ve decided to start a simple new &amp;ldquo;hobby project&amp;rdquo; that I&amp;rsquo;m calling &lt;strong&gt;Spockify&lt;/strong&gt;. The idea is that I&amp;rsquo;ll present a relatively simple web-based UI that will allow a Spotify user to log in and build new playlists based on track features like &amp;ldquo;danceability&amp;rdquo;, &amp;ldquo;tempo&amp;rdquo;, &amp;ldquo;genre&amp;rdquo;, and whatever else makes sense. I&amp;rsquo;m thinking that the base set of tracks will be the user&amp;rsquo;s saved (or liked) tracks. From there, I can use the Spotify API to get various bits of metadata for each track and then allow filtering on that metadata to build a list of songs that can be saved as a playlist.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
